  'ex.heat_legend_plume': 'Darker blue means more hours: between {start} and {stop}, the hours when the point is dark but ejecta above it could be sunlit and observable from at least one Turkish observatory (colour scale 0 to ≈{max} h, the whole-surface 99.5th percentile; smoothed by about 4°). Geometry only; whether ejecta actually rise that high is a separate question.',
